{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1451","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E2. Bitwise Queries (Hard Version)"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only difference between the easy and hard versions is the constraints on the number of queries."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is an interactive problem."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ridbit has a hidden array $$$a$$$ of $$$n$$$ integers which he wants Ashish to guess. Note that $$$n$$$ is a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"power of two"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Ashish is allowed to ask three different types of queries. They are of the form "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"AND"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$i$$$ $$$j$$$: ask for the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#AND"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise AND"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of elements $$$a_i$$$ and $$$a_j$$$ $$$(1 \\leq i, j \\le n$$$, $$$i \\neq j)$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"OR"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$i$$$ $$$j$$$: ask for the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#OR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise OR"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of elements $$$a_i$$$ and $$$a_j$$$ $$$(1 \\leq i, j \\le n$$$, $$$i \\neq j)$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"XOR"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$i$$$ $$$j$$$: ask for the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#XOR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise XOR"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of elements $$$a_i$$$ and $$$a_j$$$ $$$(1 \\leq i, j \\le n$$$, $$$i \\neq j)$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Can you help Ashish guess the elements of the array?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this version, each element takes a value in the range $$$[0, n-1]$$$ (inclusive) and Ashish can ask no more than $$$n+1$$$ queries."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains one integer $$$n$$$ $$$(4 \\le n \\le 2^{16})$$$ — the length of the array. It is guaranteed that $$$n$$$ is a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"power of two"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"custom","title":"Interaction"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Interaction"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To ask a query print a single line containing one of the following (without quotes) "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"AND i j"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"OR i j"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"XOR i j"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" where $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$ $$$(1 \\leq i, j \\le n$$$, $$$i \\neq j)$$$ denote the indices being queried."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each query, you will receive an integer $$$x$$$ whose value depends on the type of query. If the indices queried are invalid or you exceed the number of queries however, you will get $$$x = -1$$$. In this case, you should terminate the program immediately."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"When you have guessed the elements of the array, print a single line \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"!"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" \" (without quotes), followed by $$$n$$$ space-separated integers  — the elements of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Guessing the array does "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"not"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" count towards the number of queries asked."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The interactor is not adaptive."}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" The array $$$a$$$ does not change with queries."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After printing a query do not forget to output the end of the line and flush the output. Otherwise, you will get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Idleness limit exceeded"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". To do this, use:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fflush(stdout)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in C++;"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"System.out.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Java;"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flush(output)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Pascal;"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"stdout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Python;"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" see the documentation for other languages."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Hacks"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To hack the solution, use the following test format:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"On the first line print a single integer $$$n$$$ $$$(4 \\le n \\le 2^{16})$$$ — the length of the array. It "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"must"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" be a power of 2. The next line should contain $$$n$$$ space-separated integers in the range $$$[0, n-1]$$$ — the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n\n0\n\n2\n\n3\n\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nOR 1 2\n\nOR 2 3\n\nXOR 2 4\n\n! 0 0 2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The array $$$a$$$ in the example is $$$[0, 0, 2, 3]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E2","problemCode":"1451E2","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1451/problem/E2"}